Boundary decision (locked design):
  entra-id = PLATFORM / TENANT-ADMIN skill. Owns: tenant architecture, Conditional Access,
  PIM, Identity Protection, Entra Connect / Cloud Sync / hybrid identity, B2B/B2C external
  identities, Entra ID Governance (access reviews, entitlement management, lifecycle workflows).
  Does NOT own app-registration lifecycle. The existing vault skill "entra-app-lifecycle" owns
  app type -> OAuth flow, MSAL integration, service principal creation, API permission grants,
  and the credential ladder. Where upstream content touched "app registrations / service
  principals / managed identities", entra-id skill keeps it BRIEF and cross-references
  entra-app-lifecycle for the depth. The When not to use section, the Cross-references section,
  and multiple inline notes all state this boundary explicitly.

